# p_2a7c — Omar's glasses roam the house: bathroom, desk, armchair, TV stand

Omar's glasses are the most mobile personal object in the house. The sightings trace a clear daily arc: at 03:00 they are on the nightstand (×2); at 07:00 they are on the bathroom shelf (×2) — he is washing his face or brushing his teeth; at 11:00 they are at desk_o1 (working); at 16:00 they are back on the nightstand (brief break); at 18:00 they are at desk_o1 again (evening work or reading); at 21:00 they are on the armchair (settling in for TV); at 22:00 they are split between the TV stand and the armchair (falling asleep on the couch). No existing document tracks this multi-stop journey. The glasses are at five different receptacles across the day.

What sets this apart: no other document predicts glasses_omar at the bathroom shelf in the morning, at the desk during work, AND at the armchair in the evening. p_a1b2 and p_f4a7 keep them at nightstand_b1 all day.

